{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Land PR #127 through Gerrit: pypandoc-binary 1.17 + ruff 0.16.2; mcp 2.0 deferred to 732b\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nGitHub is a read-only mirror: dependabot PRs can never merge there; content is re-applied\nlocally and landed as a Gerrit change, then the PR closed by hand. PR #127 (\"deps: bump the\nuv-lock group across 1 directory with 3 updates\", branch `dependabot/uv/uv-lock-dd93acce05`)\nproposes:\n\n* `pypandoc-binary` `1.15` -> `1.17` — pinned EXACTLY (`wiki` extra + `dev` group): the\n  byte-safety tests assert byte-level pandoc output.\n* `ruff` `0.16.1` -> `0.16.2` — pinned EXACTLY in `dev` (hook, local lint, CI identical).\n* `mcp` `1.29.0` -> `2.0.0` (major), loosening the pyproject ceiling `<2` -> `<3`.\n\nThe `mcp` half is the THIRD re-proposal (PRs #124, #125, #127). It was rejected on\nevidence under ticket 1dfd (mcp 2.0 removes `mcp.server.fastmcp`, imported by\n`src/rebar/mcp_server.py` and `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py`); the migration is tracked as\nopen epic `732b-51df-acf2-477b` (bared-nickel-insect), whose migrate-vs-defer analysis\nrecommends staying on `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` until 2.0.x stabilizes. PR #125 applied the same\nrule (ticket carnivoral-consistent-lhasaapso, change 1483). This ticket lands only the\nsafe subset.\n\n## Approach\n\nLand the **safe subset** of PR #127 — the `pypandoc-binary` and `ruff` bumps — leaving the\n`mcp` ceiling at `<2` so the resolver keeps 1.29.0. In a fresh worktree (`../deps-bump`)\nbranched from current `origin/main`:\n\n1. Edit `pyproject.toml`: `pypandoc-binary==1.15` -> `==1.17` in BOTH the `wiki` extra\n   and the `dev` group (the notice test enforces one distinct pin value);\n   `ruff==0.16.1` -> `==0.16.2` in `dev`. Keep both pins exact.\n2. `uv lock --upgrade-package pypandoc-binary --upgrade-package ruff` so `uv.lock` is\n   regenerated by uv, never hand-edited (CI gates on `uv lock --check`); then sync the\n   venv so the new wheels are installed.\n3. **pandoc provenance (NOTICE)**: determine the new BUNDLED pandoc version empirically\n   (`pypandoc.get_pandoc_version()`). If it differs from 3.6.1, update `NOTICE` (the\n   `Version:` line and the `pypandoc-binary==1.15` wheel reference) and the\n   version-string assertion in `tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py` (the\n   `\"3.6.1\" in text` line) so the GPL provenance record matches what ships. Do NOT touch\n   the upstream-URL assertion (`\"pandoc.org\" in text or ...`) — a parallel change owns\n   that exact line; the two diffs must rebase cleanly past each other.\n4. **Byte-safety corpus (the load-bearing consumer of the shipped binary)**: the DC wiki\n   renderer's baseline pins the installed pandoc exactly:\n   `scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` freezes `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION = \"3.6.1\"`\n   and a per-platform `SUPPORTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256` map (darwin-arm64 + linux-x86_64);\n   `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py::test_the_installed_pandoc_matches_the_legacy_fixture_provenance`\n   validates the installed binary's version + SHA-256 against the provenance embedded in\n   `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.json` and the three\n   `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_replay/` files. Bumping the wheel means deliberately\n   re-establishing the reviewed baseline (the act the generator's docstring sanctions):\n   a. Update `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION` to the new bundled version.\n   b. Recompute BOTH fingerprints: darwin-arm64 = SHA-256 of the locally installed\n      pandoc; linux-x86_64 = download the exact `pypandoc_binary` 1.17 manylinux x86_64\n      wheel recorded (URL + hash) in `uv.lock`, extract, hash the `pandoc` inside — no\n      Linux host needed; wheel integrity is attested by uv.lock.\n   c. Regenerate the legacy manifest + three replay files with\n      `python scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` (supported binaries of one\n      version emit byte-identical fixtures, so a darwin regeneration is valid for CI's\n      linux gate; the provenance test enforces this).\n   d. Confirm with the script's non-writing `--check` and the full\n      `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py` module.\n   If the regenerated bytes churn implausibly (unit count deviates from 884, or `--check`\n   disagrees after regeneration), STOP and defer the pypandoc half too (land ruff alone)\n   rather than commit an unreviewed baseline.\n5. **ruff verdict drift**: run `make lint`; if 0.16.2 flags existing code or reformats\n   files, apply the minimal fix and note it in the commit message. NEVER touch\n   `.github/complexity-baseline.json`.\n6. Do NOT touch the `mcp` constraints, `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml`, or ADR 0050 —\n   those are 732b's edit-set.\n7. Verify (`make lint && make typecheck`, `pytest tests/unit`, the generator's `--check`),\n   commit with a `rebar-ticket:` trailer + DCO sign-off, push\n   `git push gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main`, and leave the ticket `in_progress` while the\n   orchestrator shepherds `LLM-Review` and `Verified`; close only after the change merges\n   and PR #127 is closed with a comment pointing the mcp half at 732b.\n\n## Scope\n\n* `pyproject.toml` — the two `pypandoc-binary==` pins (`wiki` + `dev`) and the `ruff==`\n  pin in `dev`.\n* `uv.lock` — regenerated `pypandoc-binary`/`ruff` entries + incidental `uv lock` churn.\n* `NOTICE` + `tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py` — only if the bundled pandoc\n  version changed (expected), and never the upstream-URL assertion line.\n* `scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py` — `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION` and both\n  `SUPPORTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256` entries, nothing else in the script.\n* `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.json` and the three files under\n  `tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_replay/` — regenerated wholesale by the generator, never\n  hand-edited.\n* Minimal source fixes ONLY if ruff 0.16.2 changes a lint/format verdict on existing code.\n* OUT: the `mcp` 1.29.0 -> 2.0.0 bump and its `<2` -> `<3` ceiling move (deferred to epic\n  `732b-51df-acf2-477b` / bared-nickel-insect — already filed, so no new ticket is needed);\n  `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml`; ADR 0050; `.github/complexity-baseline.json`;\n  dependabot configuration; any other open dependency PR.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: `pyproject.toml` has `pypandoc-binary==1.17` (twice: `wiki` + `dev`) and\n  `ruff==0.16.2`, and still has `mcp>=1.28.1,<2` in both the `mcp` extra and `dev` —\n  checked with `grep -nE 'pypandoc-binary==|ruff==|mcp>=' pyproject.toml`.\n- [ ] AC2: `uv.lock` records `pypandoc-binary` 1.17, `ruff` 0.16.2, and `mcp` 1.29.0 —\n  checked with `grep -A1 -E '^name = \"(pypandoc-binary|ruff|mcp)\"$' uv.lock` — and\n  `uv lock --check` exits 0 (the same gate CI runs).\n- [ ] AC3: `NOTICE` names the pandoc version actually bundled by 1.17 (verified via\n  `pypandoc.get_pandoc_version()` in the synced venv) and references\n  `pypandoc-binary==1.17`; `pytest tests/unit/test_notice_records_pandoc_gpl.py` exits 0.\n- [ ] AC4: the byte-safety baseline is re-established: `LEGACY_PANDOC_VERSION` + both\n  `SUPPORTED_PANDOC_BINARY_SHA256` fingerprints match the 1.17 wheels (darwin from the\n  installed binary, linux from the uv.lock-pinned manylinux x86_64 wheel), the fixtures\n  are regenerated by the script (never hand-edited),\n  `python scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py --check` exits 0, and\n  `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py` exits 0.\n- [ ] AC5: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` exits 0 in the worktree under\n  ruff 0.16.2, `make typecheck` exits 0, and `pytest tests/unit` exits 0.\n- [ ] AC6: A Gerrit change carrying this diff exists on refs/for/main with this ticket's\n  `rebar-ticket:` trailer and a DCO sign-off — checked via `git log -1 --format=%B HEAD`\n  and the change URL printed by the push.\n- [ ] AC7: The mcp 2.0 half is NOT landed (no edit to the `mcp` constraints,\n  `_optionality.yml`, or ADR 0050 — `git diff origin/main --stat` shows none), and the\n  deferral is recorded as a ticket comment naming epic `732b-51df-acf2-477b`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786805271356886001,"uuid":"d1a095b6-b895-4975-877e-9230b6e8cea4"}